## Reproduction

```bash
git clone <repo-url> && cd prefopt-repro
pip install -e ".[train]"
python -m prefopt.train_sft --config configs/sft.yaml
python -m prefopt.train_rm  --config configs/rm.yaml
python -m prefopt.{{ 'train_' + cfg.stage }} --config configs/{{ cfg.stage }}.yaml \
    --set method.beta={{ cfg.method.beta }}
```

The exact resolved config is in `config.resolved.yaml` and the library versions
are in `environment.json`, both in this repository.

## Limitations

- Single base model at {{ cfg.model.base_model.split('-')[-2] if '-' in cfg.model.base_model else 'small' }} scale; conclusions may not transfer to larger policies.
- LoRA rather than full-parameter training, which bounds how far the policy can move.
- Judge is a single LLM; agreement with human preference was not measured on this run.
- Single preference dataset, so domain generalisation is untested.
